{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Adjust Brightness}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Adjust_Brightness}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs24 Adjust Brightness
\par \pard \plain\fs20 
\par Changing the signal to more brightness shifts all grey levels in the image to lighter levels and vice versa.
\par 
\par \b Follow these steps:\plain\fs20  
\par 
\par \pard\li445\fi-275\tx445 \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs20 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on the Contrast/Brightness \ul icon\plain\fs20 {\v ICON@SEM.HLP} \{bmc bm6.bmp\}
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Press the left mouse button and adjust brightness moving the mouse left/right
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Press the \b <TAB>\plain\fs20  key \{bmc bm7.bmp\} to switch sensitivity
\par 
\par \{bmc bm8.shg\}\tab Go back
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Adjust Contrast}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Adjust_Contrast}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Adjust Brightness}
\b\fs24 Adjust Contrast
\par \pard \plain\fs20 
\par Changing the signal to more contrast expands the range of grey levels in the image and vice versa.
\par \b Follow these steps:\plain\fs20  
\par 
\par \pard\li445\fi-275\tx445 \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs20 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on  the Contrast/Brightness \ul icon\plain\fs20 {\v ICON@SEM.HLP} \{bmc bm6.bmp\}
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Press the middle mouse button and adjust contrast moving the mouse left/right.
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Press the \b <TAB>\plain\fs20  key \{bmc bm7.bmp\} to switch sensitivity
\par 
\par \{bmc bm8.shg\}\tab Go back
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Adjust Focus}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Adjust_Focus}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs24 Adjust Focus
\par \pard \plain\fs20 
\par The focus is correctly adjusted when the image on the screen is sharp and clear.
\par 
\par \b Follow these steps:\plain\fs20  
\par 
\par \pard\li445\fi-275\tx445 \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs20 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on the Magnification/Focus \ul icon\plain\fs20 {\v ICON@SEM.HLP} \{bmc bm9.bmp\}
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Press the middle mouse button and focus moving the mouse left/right
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Press the \b <TAB>\plain\fs20  key \{bmc bm7.bmp\} to switch sensitivity
\par 
\par \{bmc bm8.shg\}\tab Go back
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Adjusting the Image}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Adjusting_the_Image}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Adjust Contrast}
\b\fs24 Adjusting the Image
\par \pard \plain\fs20 
\par When the electron beam is on, the image can be generated.
\par 
\par \b What do you want to do?\plain\fs20  
\par 
\par \pard\li445\fi-275\tx445 \{bmc bm10.shg\}\tab Adjust focus
\par \{bmc bm11.shg\}\tab Select a detector
\par \{bmc bm12.shg\}\tab Adjust brightness of the image
\par \{bmc bm13.shg\}\tab Adjust contrast of the image
\par \{bmc bm14.shg\}\tab Select magnification
\par \{bmc bm15.shg\}\tab Select scan
\par 
\par \{bmc bm16.shg\}\tab Proceed
\par 
\par \{bmc bm17.shg\}\tab Go back
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Annotate the Image}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Annotate_the_Image}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn\tx445 \b\fs24 Annotate the Image
\par \pard\tx445 \plain\fs20 The data zone is used to display current parameters, including a micron marker showing the base magnification.
\par \pard\tx445 
\par \pard\tx445 \b Follow these steps:\plain\fs20  
\par \pard\tx445 
\par \pard\li445\fi-275\tx445 \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Type \b <CTRL + A>\plain\fs20  to display the annotation/measurement toolbar
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab With \b <CTRL + D>\plain\fs20  switch on the \uldb data zone\plain\fs20 {\v J3NDYE@SEM.HLP}
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Typing \b <CTRL + D>\plain\fs20  again switches the data zone off
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab With \b <CTRL + T>\plain\fs20  switch on the text input dialog
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab When text input is finished with \b OK\plain\fs20  \ul drag\plain\fs20 {\v DRAG@SEM.HLP} the text with the mouse to the exact position in the image
\par 
\par \{bmc bm3.shg\}\tab Go back
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Change the Spacer}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Change_the_Spacer}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Adjust Focus}
\b\fs24 Change the Spacer
\par \pard \plain\fs20 Different specimen heights are compensated by exchanging spacers.
\par 
\par \b Follow these steps:
\par \plain\fs20 
\par \pard\li445\fi-275\tx445 \b \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab \plain\fs20 Loosen the 3 small locating screws holding the sample holder with the hex screw driver provided and remove it.
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Loosen the 3 small locating screws holding the spacer and remove it.
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Insert new spacer and align its marks with the marks on the base ring. Tighten the 3 locating screws gently but firmly.
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Mount the sample holder, align it, and tighten the locating screws.
\par 
\par \{bmc bm18.shg\}\tab Go back\b 
\par \page
