{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Improve the Noise Level}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Improve_the_Noise_Level}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs24 Improve the Noise Level
\par \pard \plain\fs20 
\par The noise level in the image can be reduced by using longer scan times.
\par 
\par \b Follow these steps:\plain\fs20  
\par 
\par \pard\li445\fi-275\tx445 \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Click on \{bmc bm32.bmp\} to select next slower rate
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Click on Menu \b Scanning - Scan Rate\plain\fs20  to select specific slower scan rate
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Click on \{bmc bm33.bmp\} to apply \ul Frame Averaging\plain\fs20 {\v 117K7K3@tabmgr.hlp} (2 Frames). 
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Click on \{bmc bm34.bmp\} to apply \ul Frame Integration\plain\fs20 {\v EQNXF7@tabmgr.hlp} (25 frames then freeze)
\par 
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab See also \uldb SEM Control Scanning\plain\fs20 {\v R5KU.@tabmgr.hlp} and \uldb Scan Rate/Noise reduction\plain\fs20 {\v 1BUL_CS@operation.hlp} for more noise reduction
\par \pard\li445\fi-275\tx445 
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par \{bmc bm3.shg\}\tab Go back
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Initialise the Stage}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Initialise_the_Stage}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Change the Spacer}
\b\fs24 Initialise the Stage
\par \pard \plain\fs20 
\par The stage needs to be initialised before any absolute stage movement can be executed.
\par 
\par \b Follow these steps:\plain\fs20  
\par 
\par \pard\li445\fi-275\tx445 \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Select \b Stage\plain\fs20  on the Menu Bar then\b  Stage Initialise\plain\fs20  to invoke the initialisation process
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs20 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on \b OK\plain\fs20  to start initialisation
\par 
\par \{bmc bm3.shg\}\tab Go back
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Move the Specimen}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Move_the_Specimen}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs24 Move the Specimen
\par \pard \plain\fs20 The stage is moved using the \uldb Joystick\plain\fs20 {\v Contents@joystick.hlpcontents@hardpanl.hlp}.
\par Alternatively you can move a point on the image to the centre using Centre Point function
\par or move by field size using the arrow keys.
\par 
\par \b Follow these steps:\plain\fs20  (arrow key operation)
\par \pard\li445\fi-275\tx445 
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Press \{bmc bm35.bmp\},\{bmc bm36.bmp\},\{bmc bm37.bmp\},or \{bmc bm38.bmp\} for movement in the X/Y plane
\par 
\par or
\par \b Follow these steps:\plain\fs20  (centre point)
\par 
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Press \b <Ctrl + Tab>\plain\fs20  to select Centre Point
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Click on the feature you wish to centre
\par 
\par \{bmc bm3.shg\}\tab Go back
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Open the Chamber Door}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Open_the_Chamber_Door}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn\tx445 {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Change the Specimen}
\b\fs24 Open the Chamber Door
\par \pard\tx445 \plain\fs20 
\par \pard\tx445 The chamber door also carries the stage. 
\par \pard\tx445 
\par \pard\tx445 \b Follow these steps:
\par \pard\tx445 \plain\fs20 
\par \pard\li445\fi-275\tx445 \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Make sure that the specimen stage is low enough so that the specimen clears the  final lens.
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Unfasten the latch and carefully open the door
\par 
\par \{bmc bm18.shg\}\tab Go back
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Print the Image}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Print_the_Image}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs24 Print the Image
\par \pard \plain\fs20 
\par This function requires that a graphics printer or hardcopy unit accessory be installed on the instrument
\par 
\par \b Follow these steps:\plain\fs20  
\par \pard\li445\fi-275\tx445 
\par If you have a CP750 Printer Which copies the screen:
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Click on the \{bmc bm39.bmp\} to hide toolbar etc and move cursor off screen
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Initiate print on CP750
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Type \b <Shift + F3>\plain\fs20  to restore the User Interface
\par 
\par For Other Printers, unless your toolbar \{bmc bm39.bmp\} has been edited to use the printer:
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs20 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on the image with the right mouse button
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Click on \b Send to...
\par \plain\fs20 \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Click on \b Printer \plain\fs20 
\par \pard\li445\fi-275\tx445 \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Select parameters if necessary
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Click on \b Print\plain\fs20  button
\par \{bmc bm3.shg\}\tab Go back
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Pump the Chamber}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Pump_the_Chamber}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Close the Chamber Door}
\b\fs24 Pump the Chamber
\par \pard \plain\fs20 
\par The chamber is pumped from atmospheric pressure automatically when the Pump coomand is given.
\par 
\par \b Follow these steps:
\par \plain\fs20 
\par \pard\li445\fi-275\tx445 \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs20 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on the \{bmc bm40.bmp\} on the status bar to display commands
\par 
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs20 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on the pump command \{bmc bm41.bmp\} to start pumping\b 
\par 
\par \plain\fs20 \{bmc bm24.shg\}\tab Go back
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Put in a new Specimen}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Put_in_a_new_Specimen}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn\tx445 \b\fs24 Put in a new Specimen
\par \pard\tx445 \plain\fs20 
\par \pard\tx445 The specimen is mounted on a specimen stub. Several sizes are available.
\par \pard\tx445 
\par \pard\tx445 \b Follow these steps:\plain\fs20  
\par \pard\tx445 
\par \pard\li445\fi-275\tx445 \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Apply the forceps to a groove in the stub and insert it in the sample holder.
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Tighten the locating screw gently but firmly
\par 
\par \{bmc bm18.shg\}\tab Go back
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Record the Image}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Record_the_Image}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Contents}
\b\fs24 Record the Image
\par \pard \plain\fs20 
\par This function requires that the High Resolution Recording Unit accessory is installed on the instrument.
\par 
\par \b Follow these steps:\plain\fs20  
\par 
\par \pard\li445\fi-275\tx445 \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs20 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on the image with the right mouse button
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Click on \b Send to...
\par \plain\fs20 \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Click on \b HRRU \plain\fs20 
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Select parameters if necessary
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Click on \b Photo\plain\fs20  button
\par 
\par \{bmc bm3.shg\}\tab Go back
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Remove the Specimen}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Remove_the_Specimen}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs24 Remove the Specimen
\par \pard \plain\fs20 
\par The specimen is usually mounted on a stub. This stub is clamped to the stage with a locating screw.
\par 
\par \b Follow these steps:
\par \plain\fs20 
\par \pard\li445\fi-275\tx445 \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Loosen the small locating screw holding the specimen stub in position with the hex screw driver provided.
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Apply the forceps to the groove in the stub and pull it out of the stage
\par 
\par \{bmc bm18.shg\}\tab Go back
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Save the Image}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Save_the_Image}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Display Control Panel}
\b\fs24 Save the Image
\par \pard \plain\fs20 The photo number can be added to the name under which the image is stored. Photo number must be selected from the Export TIFF dialog under Settings/Filename/Format.
\par 
\par \b Follow these steps:\plain\fs20  
\par \pard\li445\fi-275\tx445 \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Save the image by \ul clicking\plain\fs20 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on the Export TIFF \ul icon\plain\fs20 {\v ICON@SEM.HLP} \{bmc bm42.bmp\} with the left mouse button
\par \b or:\plain\fs20 
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab  Click with the right mouse button on the image, select \b Send To\plain\fs20  and the destination (e.g.\b  TIFF File \plain\fs20 ) to display the setup dialog  for the image export.
\par 
\par \{bmc bm3.shg\}\tab Go back
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Screening and Final Touches}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Screening_and_Final_Touches}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs24 Screening and Final Touches
\par \pard \plain\fs20 Move the specimen to investigate it's features from different points of view. Add data to the image (annotation) and take a micrograph (save, record or print it).
\par 
\par \b What do you want to do?\plain\fs20 
\par \pard\li445\fi-275\tx445 \b 
\par \{bmc bm43.shg\}\tab \plain\fs20 Initialise the stage 
\par \{bmc bm44.shg\}\tab Move the specimen
\par \{bmc bm45.shg\}\tab Improve noise level
\par \{bmc bm46.shg\}\tab Annotate the image
\par \{bmc bm47.shg\}\tab Save the image
\par \{bmc bm48.shg\}\tab Record the image
\par \{bmc bm49.shg\}\tab Print the image\b 
\par \plain\fs20 
\par \{bmc bm50.shg\}\tab Proceed
\par \{bmc bm51.shg\}\tab Go back
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Select Magnification}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Select_Magnification}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn\tx445 \b\fs24 Select Magnification
\par \pard\tx445 \plain\fs20 
\par \pard\tx445 Choose magnification as required. Start at low magnification.
\par \pard\tx445 
\par \pard\tx445 \b Follow these steps:\plain\fs20  
\par \pard\tx445 
\par \pard\li445\fi-275\tx445 \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs20 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on the Magnification/Focus \ul icon\plain\fs20 {\v ICON@SEM.HLP} \{bmc bm9.bmp\}
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Press the left mouse button and adjust magnification moving the mouse left/right
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Press the \b <TAB>\plain\fs20  key \{bmc bm7.bmp\} to switch sensitivity
\par 
\par \{bmc bm8.shg\}\tab Go back
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Select Scan}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Select_Scan}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn\tx445 \b\fs24 Select Scan
\par \pard\tx445 \plain\fs20 Selection of the scan rate can greatly influence the quality of the image
\par \pard\tx445 
\par \pard\tx445 \b Follow these steps:\plain\fs20  
\par \pard\li445\fi-275\tx445 
\par 
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Click on \{bmc bm32.bmp\} to select next slower rate
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Click on \{bmc bm52.bmp\} to select next faster rate
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Click on Menu \b Scanning - Scan Rate\plain\fs20  to select specific scan rate
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Click on Reduced Raster icon \{bmc bm53.bmp\} for higher repetition rate for critical adjustment(clicking again will revert to Normal Mode)
\par 
\par \{bmc bm8.shg\}\tab Go back
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Select a Detector}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Select_a_Detector}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Improve the Noise Level;Initialise the Stage}
\b\fs24 Select a Detector
\par \pard \plain\fs20 
\par \pard\li445\fi-275\tx445 
\par Select the required detector from the Main Menu under \b Detection - Detectors
\par \plain\fs20 The selected detector is marked by a tick 
\par Click on the required Detector \{bmc bm54.bmp\}
\par 
