{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Shut down the Instrument}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Shut_down_the_Instrument}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs24 Shut down the Instrument
\par \pard \plain\fs20 Exit shuts the current User Interface down
\par Log Off closes all User interfaces.
\par In both these cases the server continues to run.
\par 
\par \b Follow these steps:\plain\fs20 
\par \pard\li445\fi-275\tx445 \b 
\par \plain\fs20 \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Type \b <ALT + F>\plain\fs20  to access the File menu and then\b  <G> \plain\fs20 to start logging off
\par \b or:
\par \plain\fs20 \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Type \b <ALT + F4>\plain\fs20  to start Exit
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs20 {\v CLICK@SEM.HLP} on the \b YES\plain\fs20  button to proceed the shut down process
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Save the system conditions with clicking on \b YES\plain\fs20  button
\par 
\par To shut down the server right click on \{bmc bm55.bmp\} in the task bar and select \b Close
\par If the server does not close another LEO application is still running.
\par \pard\li445\fi-275\tx445 
\par \cf1 Windows Must be Shut Down before switching off power\plain\b\fs20 
\par \plain\fs20 
\par \{bmc bm50.shg\}\tab Go back
\par \{bmc bm4.shg\}\tab Quit help\b 
