{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Beam Setup}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Beam_Setup}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \plain\fs36 Beam Setup
\par \pard \fs24 For correct imaging the filament current must be correctly set and the beam aligned
\par With the \b Beam On\plain\fs24  proceed as follows:
\par \pard\li445\fi-275\tx445 \fs20 \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Display the \uldb Control Panel\plain\fs20 {\v Contents@tabmgr.hlp} by typing <Ctrl + G>
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Select the \uldb Signal Tab\plain\fs20 {\v 1OTG14F@tabmgr.hlp} and ensure Auto Brightness is off by clicking both Off buttons
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Adjust Brightness and Contrast to suitable levels using the Scroll bars
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab Select the \uldb Gun Tab\plain\fs20 {\v 5_0HOO@tabmgr.hlp}  click or double click on entries to change them (Beam Current typically 400 MicroA, EHT Target, I Probe )
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab \uldb Set the filament Current\plain\fs20 {\v 13HR49B@operation.hlp}
\par \pard\li445\fi-275\tx445 \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab \uldb Align the Beam\plain\fs20 {\v 1LKD_PL@operation.hlp}
\par \{bmc bm5.bmp\}\tab \uldb Check the filament current setting\plain\fs20 {\v 13HR49B@operation.hlp}
\par 
\par See also:
\par \uldb Setting EHT And probe Current\plain\fs20 {\v 1N48D_S@operation.hlpSetting_EHT_and_Spot_Size@operation.hlp}
\par 
\par \uldb Adjusting the variable aperture\plain\fs20 {\v 334XEAC@operation.hlp}
\par 
\par \{bmc bm51.shg\}\tab Proceed
